[2026-06-21] PHASE: INVESTIGATE | root cause | OK
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ROOT CAUSE (single bug, all three years): merge_passes.py n_for() extracts the FIRST
4-digit year from the dir basename via regex production-(\d{4}). The biennium-named
transition dirs hold the ODD-year regular session, but the regex grabs the EVEN leading
year, so the merge capped at the WRONG (tiny even-year) oracle N:
  production-1900-01 -> regex 1900 -> ORACLE[1900]=15   => merged capped at 15
  production-1907-09 -> regex 1907 -> ORACLE[1907]=539  => merged capped at 539
  production-1910-11 -> regex 1910 -> ORACLE[1910]=1    => merged capped at 1
The full session text ALREADY EXISTED in parsed_acts_certified.json (and repaired/
recovered/multiengine) in each dir; only the merge step was under-built due to the
wrong cap. Confirmed by input inventory (distinct chapters <= true N):
